  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Demand Forecasting & Backlog Management for an industrial distributor selling 20 MRO/OEM SKUs across fasteners, bearings, valves, electrical, and safety into MRO, OEM, Contractor, and Government segments. Stakeholders include the Category Manager (forecast accuracy, mix), Supply Planner (backlog, lead time), Branch Manager (fill rate, satisfaction), and CFO (open-order value, backorder exposure).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Forecast accuracy / MAPE = avg_forecast_error (forecast_error_pct); best-in-class industrial distributors: 10-20% MAPE\n- Forecast bias = forecasted_units - actual_units; persistent positive bias indicates over-forecast and inventory build\n- Fill rate = fill_rate_pct on sales_orders; MRO target ≥97%\n- Backorder volume = backorder_units (sales_orders) and backordered_count of orders (demand_kpi_monthly)\n- Open-order value = open_order_value_usd; revenue-at-risk in the pipeline\n- Lead time = lead_time_days (promised); compare to avg_days_to_ship for commitment vs. actual\n- Customer satisfaction = customer_satisfaction_score (1-5); <3.5 is a churn warning\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - demand_kpi_monthly (source: product_skus) — dims: order_date, product_category, customer_segment, order_status; measures: total_order_revenue, total_order_quantity, total_order_count, backordered_count, avg_lead_time, max_order_quantity.\n  - forecast_accuracy_monthly (source: demand_forecasts) — dims: forecast_month, product_category, model_version; measures: total_forecasted_units, total_actual_units, avg_forecast_error, forecast_count, over_forecast_count, max_forecasted_units.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. sku, product_name, open_order_value_usd, fill_rate_pct, customer_satisfaction_score).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly total order revenue by product category for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which product categories have the worst forecast accuracy (highest avg forecast error) over the last 6 months?",
    "Top 10 SKUs by open order value USD this week — and what is their fill rate?",
    "How has the monthly backordered order count trended across customer segments?",
    "Which SKUs have the largest forecast bias (forecasted vs actual units) in the latest model version?",
    "What is the average lead time and days-to-ship by customer segment for shipped orders?",
    "Which product categories have customer satisfaction below 3.5, and what is their backorder volume?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest order quantity?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(max_order_quantity) AS max_order_quantity",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total order revenue usd changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT order_date, MEASURE(total_order_revenue) AS total_order_revenue",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY order_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest forecasted units?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, MEASURE(max_forecasted_units) AS max_forecasted_units",
        "FROM {fqn}.forecast_accuracy_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest forecasted units changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, MEASURE(max_forecasted_units) AS max_forecasted_units",
        "FROM {fqn}.forecast_accuracy_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total units ordered break down by product sku code for 'Backordered' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT sku, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(order_quantity) AS total_order_quantity",
        "FROM {fqn}.product_skus",
        "WHERE order_status = 'Backordered' GROUP BY sku ORDER BY total_order_quantity DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total total open order value in usd over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(open_order_value_usd) AS total_open_order_value_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.sales_orders",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average absolute forecast error percent changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, AVG(forecast_error_pct) AS avg_forecast_error_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts",
        "GROUP BY forecast_month ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
